<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1649" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">āh</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ā</span></b>  (v. Neue, Formenl. II. 812), interj.
		 [acc. to <i><span class="en">Prisc. 570</span></i> P.
		contract. from aha], <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>ah! alas! ha! ah me!</i> an exclamation. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Of pain or grief, Gr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἴ, αἴ</span>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ah, nescis quam doleam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					Heaut. 5, 1, 61</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Verg. E. 1, 15</span></i>.
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Of entreaty
			to avert an evil: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ah! noli,</span>”
				<i>do not</i>, <i>I pray!</i>
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Am. 1, 3, 22</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b> Of
			indignation or reproach: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ah stulte,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					Ad. 4, 7, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ah, rogitas?</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					And. 5, 1, 9</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">3, 1, 11</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>IV.</b> Of admonition: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ah, ne me obsecra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					And. 3, 3, 11</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ah desine,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 5, 6, 8</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>V.</b> Of
			consolation: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quid? ah volet, certo scio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					Eun. 5, 2, 50</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>VI.</b> Of
			raillery or joy, <i><span class="en">Plaut. Curc. 1, 2, 39</span></i>.</div>
